      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In chaotic situations like this, it's often best to avoid the main rush, which is where the most panicked travelers congregate. Don't rely solely on the screens; sometimes the information displayed is just as unreliable as a glitching app. If you can, head to an airline service desk or a dedicated customer support area, even if it means waiting in line, because they have the most up-to-date, albeit slow, information.\n\nYou should watch out for airlines that are currently experiencing high volumes of cancellations, as they might be the ones with the most unpredictable schedules. It's a bit like trying to navigate a swarm of very stressed-out, disorganized traffic. Sometimes, a smaller, less prominent airline might have a more stable schedule right now, even if it takes a slightly different route.\n\nRemember, when things are this chaotic, the best strategy is often to be proactive, not reactive. Don't just wait for the next announcement; actively seek out alternative options yourself. You've got to be more nimble than the general crowd!",
      "source": "target",
