      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While \"gremlins\" is a fun, evocative term, the technical reality you're describing—where software behaves erratically and unpredictably—is usually categorized under terms like \"software instability,\" \"bugs,\" or \"system anomalies.\" If the glitches seem targeted or patterned, you might be looking at something more serious like a denial-of-service attack, but for a standard travel app, it's usually just a massive overload or a poorly coded update.\n\nIt's certainly frustrating when technology acts like it has a mischievous streak! Sometimes, when a system is under immense strain, it starts throwing errors that look like intentional chaos, which is just the digital equivalent of a very clumsy, very angry goblin trying to trip you up. Just try to treat the app like a very unreliable, slightly possessed piece of machinery.\n\nIn short, stick to the basics: if the app is acting like it's possessed by a tiny, digital imp, ignore it and look for a human source of truth, like a physical counter. You need reliable data, not digital mischief!",
